# Try the API from VS Code (REST Client extension) or Visual Studio.
# Start it first:  dotnet run --project backend/TruckGo.Api

@api = http://localhost:5000/api/v1

### Log in (demo driver)
# @name login
POST {{api}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "test1", "pin": "1234", "deviceId": "dev-pc" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.accessToken}}

### Trucks and trailers
GET {{api}}/vehicles
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Deliveries of the demo truck
GET {{api}}/trucks/AB-1234/deliveries
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### One delivery, with its 1st and 2nd weight
GET {{api}}/deliveries/QN2/421987
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The driver chooses a new PIN (asked by the app when login says "mustChangePin": true)
POST {{api}}/auth/change-pin
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "currentPin": "1234", "newPin": "4821" }

### The app sends GPS points (a batch; sending the same clientId again stores nothing twice)
POST {{api}}/positions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

[
  { "clientId": "6f1c2a1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "truckPlate": "AB-1234", "latitude": 52.5545, "longitude": -1.5260, "recordedAt": "2026-10-11T08:00:00Z", "accuracyM": 8, "speedKmh": 0, "plantCode": "QN2", "deliveryNumber": "422211" },
  { "clientId": "6f1c2a1e-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "truckPlate": "AB-1234", "latitude": 52.5560, "longitude": -1.5240, "recordedAt": "2026-10-11T08:01:00Z", "accuracyM": 8, "speedKmh": 34, "plantCode": "QN2", "deliveryNumber": "422211" }
]
